  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 102.36 “Ceiling limit value” means a concentration of a regulated air toxic pollutant that if exceeded during any part of a working exposure, will cause detrimental effects to humans.\n\nSource. #6328, INTERIM, eff 8-24-96, EXPIRED: 12-22-96\n\nNew. #6468-A, eff 3-5-97; renumbered by #8256 (from Env-A 101.61), (see Revision Note #1 at chapter heading); renumbered by #8304 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading); renumbered by #9839 (from Env-A 101.36), (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading); ss by #13105, eff 9-25-20 (formerly Env-A 101.37) (see Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-A 100)",
